        headlines: ["Driver Rolls Away With Trooper's Arm in the Window", "Self-Styled Traveler Charged After Parking Lot Dragging"],
        law: "resisting",
        threshold: 7,
        spec: "Resisted, delayed and obstructed a law enforcement officer in the discharge of official duties, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: false,
        summary: "A highway trooper stopped {D} on {DATE} for no brake light. {DL} rolled the window down two inches, called the trooper a stranger with no authority, and refused to hand over papers. When the trooper reached in to unlock the door, {DL} accelerated. The trooper was pulled along for twenty feet and hurt a shoulder. {DL} says {D.he} panicked when a hand came through the window.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Dash Camera", "The trooper reaches in and the car lurches forward."), E(.forensic, 2, "Shoulder X-Ray", "A sprained shoulder consistent with being dragged."), E(.document, 2, "Citation", "No license on file and expired registration."), E(.statement, 1, "Roadside Words", "{DL} says laws do not apply to travelers.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Panic", "{DL} says a hand came in without warning.")],
        role: "Highway patrol trooper",
        exam: [.direct("Why did you stop {D}?", "\"For no brake light. It was a routine traffic stop on a highway, at an ordinary hour.\""), .direct("What did the defendant do when you approached?", "\"Rolled the window down two inches, called me a stranger with no authority, and refused to hand over papers.\""), .direct("Why did you reach in?", "\"To unlock the door after repeated refusals. I said I was opening the door, and I put my arm in.\""), .direct("What happened next?", "\"The car moved and I was pulled along for about twenty feet. I was hurt, and I fell away from the car.\""), .direct("What did the defendant say at the roadside?", "\"That laws do not apply to travelers. {D} said it more than once.\""), .direct("What did the citation show?", "\"No license on file and expired registration. Those were added to the charges.\""), .cross("Did you give a warning?", "\"I said I was opening the door. I did not say what would happen if {D.he} did not open it.\""), .cross("Was the defendant speeding at the end?", "\"Not at the end. The car lurched forward and then stopped a short distance later.\""), .cross("Did the defendant resist beyond that?", "\"No. {D.He} stopped the car and got out when ordered.\""), .cross("What was your injury?", "\"A sprained shoulder consistent with being dragged. It healed in a few weeks.\""), .cross("Did the dash camera show everything?", "\"It shows my arm going in and the car lurching. It does not show the pedals.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} refused to comply and drove off with a trooper's arm in the window.", "A panicked reaction to an unexpected hand."),
        allocution: "\"I overreacted.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} had posted online about driving away if stopped.", "{DL}'s foot slipped from the brake when the trooper grabbed {D.him}."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you drive off on purpose?", "\"No. A hand came through the window, and I panicked. The car moved, and I did not mean it to.\""), .direct("Why did you refuse to hand over papers?", "\"I misread some online advice. I thought I did not have to give documents to a roadside stop.\""), .direct("What about the roadside words?", "\"Words on a screen. I was repeating things I had read, and I did not understand them.\""), .direct("Why did you speed up?", "\"My foot slipped. I was frightened, and my foot slipped off the brake onto the gas.\""), .direct("Did you know the trooper was hurt?", "\"Not at the time. I did not know until I stopped, and I was horrified.\""), .direct("What do you want the trooper to know?", "\"I truly am sorry. I never meant to hurt you, and I was wrong about my rights.\""), .cross("You called the trooper a stranger with no authority, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I said it because of what I read. It was foolish.\""), .cross("The car lurched when the trooper reached in, didn't it?", "\"Yes. My foot slipped, and the car moved.\""), .cross("You dragged a trooper twenty feet, didn't you?", "\"The car did. I did not mean it, and I apologize.\""), .cross("You had no license on file, did you?", "\"No. I let it lapse, and I should not have been driving.\""), .cross("You refused the trooper's repeated requests, didn't you?", "\"Yes, because I was wrong and frightened.\"")],
        openings: ("A trooper stopped {D} for no brake light, and {D} rolled the window down two inches, called the trooper a stranger with no authority, and refused papers. When the trooper reached in to unlock the door, the car lurched forward and dragged the trooper twenty feet.", "{D} panicked when a hand came through the window, and {D}'s foot slipped. A frightened driver who misread online advice is not someone who set out to hurt a trooper."),
        closings: ("Repeated refusals, a hand in the window, and a car that accelerated and pulled the trooper twenty feet. {D} knew a trooper was at the door.", "A hand through a window, a slipped foot, and a bad idea read online. The State must prove {D} drove off on purpose to hurt a trooper."),
