        openings: ("{V}, 13, and a 14-year-old friend were riding bikes on a greenway when a rider on a green bike followed them into the trail, and their bodies were found the next morning. Six years later DNA on a shoelace used to bind a wrist led by family tree to {D}, who owned a matching green bike.", "The bike and the shoelace were stolen from {D}'s garage the spring before. DNA can travel with a stolen object, and a cellmate who wants a deal will say what a prosecutor needs."),
        closings: ("A rider on a green bike, a knotted lace with {D}'s DNA, a matching bike registration, and a cellmate who heard the details. The evidence points to {D}.", "A broken garage window, a stolen bike, and a cellmate trading a story for a deal. The State must prove {D} was on that trail."),
        timeline: [(0, "4:15 p.m.: the teens enter the trail."), (0, "4:20 p.m.: the rider follows."), (1, "The bodies are found."), (2300, "The retest and the tree search.")],
