        exam: [.direct("What do you do as a homicide detective?", "\"I investigate killings. I examine scenes, autopsies, digital evidence, and surveillance, and I interview witnesses and the people involved.\""), .direct("What did you find at {V}'s home?", "\"Two days after {DATE}, a coworker used a spare key to check on {V}, a 31-year-old barber who had missed shifts, and found {V} dead in the bathtub.\""), .direct("What did the autopsy show?", "\"Nineteen stab wounds, defensive cuts on the hands, and a gunshot to the head. {V} fought back, and then {V} was shot.\""), .direct("What did {V}'s smartwatch record?", "\"A fall alert and the end of a heartbeat at 6:41 p.m. That gave us a time to build the investigation around.\""), .direct("How did {D} become a suspect?", "\"A bloody towel held DNA from {D}, {V}'s former partner. A plate reader caught {DL}'s car near the home at 6:10 p.m.\""), .direct("What did the defendant's searches show?", "\"Searches for how to clean blood and where {V} would be that evening. They were made before the killing.\""), .direct("What did the defendant first say?", "\"{DL} first denied being there. Later, {DL} said {V} attacked {DL} after years of abuse and {DL} acted to survive.\""), .cross("Did you find messages from {V} to the defendant?", "\"Yes. Abusive messages in which {V} threatens and demeans {DL}. They are hard to read.\""), .cross("Was there a clinic note about the defendant?", "\"Yes. A note about a bruised wrist. It is consistent with {D.his} account of being held, but I cannot say how the wrist was hurt.\""), .cross("What did {D} bring to the house?", "\"A stolen handgun and a knife in a bag. {D.He} says that was for protection, and I cannot prove otherwise.\""), .cross("Did {V} pin the defendant against the vanity?", "\"{DL} says so, and that {V} pulled a knife first. I have no witness to that moment.\""), .cross("Did the defendant call for help?", "\"No. {D.He} left. The coworker found {V} two days later.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Domestic violence advocate",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Walk the jury through your work as a domestic violence advocate.", "\"I counsel survivors of abuse. I help people plan safety, and I testify about how abuse affects thinking and behavior.\""), .direct("How can long abuse affect a person's reaction in a final fight?", "\"A person may believe they will die. Fear can lead to extreme responses, and the person may keep fighting until the threat feels over.\""), .direct("Why do survivors stay or return?", "\"Fear, money, children, and hope. Leaving is the most dangerous time, and many people try several times.\""), .direct("What did you review in this case?", "\"Messages in which {V} threatens and demeans {D}, a clinic note about a bruised wrist, and {DF}'s account of the night.\""), .direct("Why might someone lie at first?", "\"Fear of not being believed, and fear of the justice system. It is common for survivors to hide the truth at first.\""), .direct("What does the number of wounds tell you?", "\"It can reflect panic and fear. It does not by itself show planning or intent, though a jury may view it differently.\""), .cross("Did you speak to {D}?", "\"Yes. I spoke with {D.him} after the arrest. I cannot say what happened that night, only what {D.he} told me.\""), .cross("Can an abuse survivor also plan a killing?", "\"Yes. It is possible. I cannot say it did not happen here. I can only explain what research shows.\""), .cross("Does the evidence include a stolen gun?", "\"Yes. {D.He} brought a stolen handgun and a knife in a bag. That is a fact I cannot explain away.\""), .cross("Did the defendant search how to clean blood?", "\"Yes. {D.He} did. That is consistent with panic, but it can also suggest an attempt to hide.\""), .cross("Did the defendant call for help?", "\"No. {D.He} did not. I cannot say why, but fear and shock can explain it.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} stabbed and shot {V}, then lied about being there.", "{D} acted in fear after years of abuse."),
        allocution: "\"I live with it every day.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} brought a stolen handgun and a knife to the house in a bag.", "{V} had pinned {DL} against the vanity and pulled a knife first."),
        defendant: [.direct("Please tell us about your relationship with {V}.", "\"We were together for years. {V} abused me, and I was afraid. I tried to leave many times, and it did not work.\""), .direct("What happened that evening?", "\"I went to the house to get my things. {V} pinned me against the vanity and pulled a knife. I was terrified.\""), .direct("What did you do?", "\"I fought back to survive. I did not plan to kill anyone. I only wanted to get away, and I acted without thinking.\""), .direct("Why did you bring a stolen handgun and a knife?", "\"I was afraid of {V}. I thought I needed protection. I know how it looks, and I know I should not have brought them.\""), .direct("Why did you first deny being there?", "\"I was scared. I thought no one would believe me, and I did not want to go to jail. I lied at first.\""), .direct("How has this affected you?", "\"Broken, more than anything. I lost someone I once loved, and I live with the fear. I wish I had been able to leave sooner.\""), .cross("You searched how to clean blood, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I did, after. I was in shock, and I did not know what to do. I know it looks bad.\""), .cross("You also searched where {V} would be that evening, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I wanted to pick up my things when {V} was out. I did not plan to hurt anyone.\""), .cross("Your DNA was on the bloody towel, wasn't it?", "\"Yes. I used it to wipe my hands. I did not know what else to do.\""), .cross("Your car was near the home at 6:10, wasn't it?", "\"Yes. I was there. I told you at first that I was not, and I am sorry for the lie.\""), .cross("Nineteen stab wounds is a lot, isn't it?", "\"Yes. I do not remember how many. I was fighting for my life, and I did not stop until it was over.\"")],
        openings: ("Two days after {DATE}, a coworker found {V}, a 31-year-old barber, dead in a bathtub with nineteen stab wounds and a gunshot to the head. DNA on a bloody towel was {D}'s, {V}'s former partner, whose car was near the home at 6:10 p.m.", "The defense will present years of abuse, threats in messages, a bruised wrist, and a final fight in which {D} feared for {D}'s life. {D} lied at first out of fear, and acted to survive."),
        closings: ("Nineteen stab wounds, a gunshot to the head, DNA on a towel, a plate reader near the home, searches for how to clean blood, and a stolen gun in a bag. The evidence shows more than a fight.", "Years of abuse, a knife pulled by {V}, and a survivor who feared for {D}'s life. The State must prove that {D} was not acting in self-defense."),
        timeline: [(-200, "{V} and {DL} separate."), (0, "6:10 p.m.: {DL}'s car near the house."), (0, "6:41 p.m.: the heartbeat ends."), (2, "A coworker finds {V}.")],
        identified: "DNA on a towel and a plate reader hit.",
        notDone: ["The gun was never recovered."],
        aggravating: ["The offense was especially heinous, atrocious, or cruel"],
        mood: .divided,
        impact: "{V} was the one who always opened the shop.",
        doctrines: ["selfDefense", "lesserIncluded"],
        genders: ["D": .female, "V": .male])

    static let neighborsMailboxV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.neighborsMailbox",
        category: .whiteCollar,
        headlines: ["Phones Charged to Retiree's Name Shipped to Package Locker", "Wireless Accounts Opened in 81-Year-Old's Identity"],
        law: "identityTheft",
        threshold: 3,
        spec: "Knowingly used identifying information of {V} to open wireless accounts and obtain goods.",
        ages: 24...40,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{V}, 81, found a collections notice for four wireless accounts and nine phones that {V.he} never opened. The phones were shipped to a package locker near {V}'s home. {D}, a neighbor who resells used electronics, picked up several of them on camera and sold matching models online. {DL} says {D.he} buys phones in bulk at liquidation sales, and that a locker pickup was for a friend.",
        state: [E(.document, 3, "Wireless Applications", "Four accounts opened with {V}'s name and number and a phone number tied to {DL}."), E(.digital, 3, "Resale Listings", "Matching phones sold under {DL}'s seller name within days."), E(.video, 2, "Locker Camera", "{DL} removes a package from the locker.")],
        defense: [E(.document, 3, "Liquidation Receipts", "Receipts for bulk phone buys from two liquidators."), E(.statement, 2, "Friend's Pickup", "A friend asked {DL} to pick up parcels."), E(.document, 1, "Phone Number", "The number on the forms is a prepaid line.")],
        role: "Fraud investigator",
        exam: [.direct("What do you do as a fraud investigator?", "\"I investigate identity theft and account fraud for wireless carriers. I trace applications, shipping addresses, and sales to the people behind them.\""), .direct("What did {V}, who is 81, find?", "\"A collections notice for four wireless accounts and nine phones that {V} never opened. {V} did not know about the accounts.\""), .direct("How did you trace the phones?", "\"They were shipped to a package locker near {V}'s home. The applications used {V}'s name and number and a phone number tied to {D}.\""), .direct("What did the locker camera show?", "\"It shows {DL} removing a package from the locker. {DL} picked up several of them on camera.\""), .direct("What did you find in the listings?", "\"Matching phones sold online under {D.his} seller name within days. The models matched those shipped to the locker.\""), .direct("What did you find in {D}'s home?", "\"A note listing {V}'s birth date and ID number. That is information used to open the accounts.\""), .cross("Does the defendant resell used electronics?", "\"Yes. {D.He} buys phones in bulk at liquidation sales. Receipts from two liquidators show those purchases.\""), .cross("Did a friend ask the defendant to pick up parcels?", "\"{DL} says so. A friend gave {DL} the locker code. The friend later turned out to own the prepaid line on the forms.\""), .cross("Is the number on the forms a prepaid line?", "\"Yes. It is a prepaid line. {DL} says it was not {DL}'s, and I traced it to the friend.\""), .cross("Could the defendant have bought matching phones legitimately?", "\"Possibly. {D.He} sells many phones. But the timing matched the locker pickups, and I cannot ignore that.\""), .cross("Did the defendant open the accounts?", "\"I cannot say. I have the forms, the locker, and the listings, and I do not have video of {DL} typing the applications.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Liquidation dealer",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Tell us about your work as a liquidation dealer.", "\"I sell electronics in bulk at liquidation auctions. Retailers and carriers send me pallets of phones and tablets, and I sell to resellers like {D}.\""), .direct("How do bulk sales work?", "\"Buyers pay for pallets of mixed phones. We give receipts, but we do not always track serial numbers by seller.\""), .direct("What did {D} buy from you?", "\"Bulk lots of phones. {D.He} bought several times and paid by check. I have receipts for those purchases.\""), .direct("Could some phones in a bulk lot be the same models as the stolen ones?", "\"Yes. Many phones are the same model. A lot can contain dozens of matching phones.\""), .direct("What do you know about the defendant's character?", "\"{DF} has been a customer for years and always paid on time. I never had a problem with {DF}.\""), .direct("Did the defendant ask about a locker?", "\"No. {D.He} never mentioned a locker. I only know {D.him} as a buyer.\""), .cross("Do your receipts show serial numbers?", "\"Not always. They list models and quantities, not each serial number. I cannot say if the phones in {D.his} listings came from me.\""), .cross("Did you sell the defendant the phones from the locker?", "\"No. I did not. I have no record of selling those phones to {D.him}.\""), .cross("Do you know anything about the accounts?", "\"No. I only know that {D.he} bought phones from me. I do not know where the others came from.\""), .cross("Did the defendant buy a lot around that time?", "\"Yes. {D.He} bought a few lots, but not an unusual amount. I did not keep a count.\""), .cross("Could {D} buy from other sources?", "\"Yes. Many resellers do. {DF} said {DF} used two liquidators, and I am one of them.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} opened phone accounts in a neighbor's name and sold the phones.", "{D} buys and resells legitimately."),
        allocution: "\"I got in over my head.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} kept a note listing {V}'s birth date and ID number.", "{DL}'s friend gave {DL} the locker code and was later found to own the prepaid line."),
        defendant: [.direct("What can you tell us about your resale business?", "\"I buy used electronics in bulk at liquidation sales and resell them online. I have receipts for many purchases.\""), .direct("Why did you pick up packages at the locker?", "\"A friend asked me to. The friend gave me the code and said they were parcels for work. I saw no harm in it.\""), .direct("Did you open accounts in {V}'s name?", "\"No. I did not. I never applied for any accounts, and I did not use {V}'s information.\""), .direct("Why did you sell matching phones?", "\"I sell many phones. Some came from my bulk buys. I did not know any were from the accounts.\""), .direct("Why did you have a note with {V}'s information?", "\"A friend gave me a note to help with a delivery. I kept it. I did not know what it was for.\""), .direct("How do you feel about {V}?", "\"I am terrible. {V} is elderly and was hurt. I did not know, and I would never have helped if I had.\""), .cross("You picked up several packages from the locker, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I did. I thought I was helping a friend, and I did not look inside.\""), .cross("The phones you sold matched the ones shipped, didn't they?", "\"Some did. I did not check where they came from, and I should have.\""), .cross("The note lists {V}'s birth date and ID number, doesn't it?", "\"Yes. I kept it. I did not know what it was for, and It looks bad, I know.\""), .cross("Your friend gave you the locker code, didn't the friend?", "\"Yes. And the friend owns the prepaid line. I did not know that until the investigators told me.\""), .cross("You never asked what was in the packages, did you?", "\"No. I did not. I should have asked, and I did not.\"")],
        openings: ("{V}, 81, found a collections notice for four wireless accounts and nine phones that {V} never opened. The phones were shipped to a package locker near {V}'s home, and {D}, a neighbor who resells used electronics, picked up several of them on camera and sold matching models online.", "The defense will present bulk buys from liquidation sales, a friend who asked for a pickup and gave the locker code, and a prepaid line owned by that friend. {D} did not open any account."),
        closings: ("Four accounts opened in {V}'s name, nine phones shipped to a locker, {D} on camera taking packages, matching phones sold online, and a note with {V}'s birth date and ID number. The trail leads to {D}.", "A reseller who buys in bulk, a friend who owned the prepaid line and gave the code, and no one who saw {D} apply. The State has not proved that {D} opened the accounts."),
        timeline: [(-90, "The first account is opened."), (-30, "Phones ship to the locker."), (0, "{V} receives a notice."), (45, "Serials match {DL}'s listings.")],
        identified: "A phone number, locker video and resale listings.",
        notDone: ["The friend was never interviewed."],
        aggravating: ["The victim was elderly"],
        mitigating: ["No prior criminal record"],
        mood: .indifferent,
        impact: "My credit was perfect for sixty years.",
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"])

    static let hotelPartyOverdoseV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.hotelPartyOverdose",
        category: .drugs,
        headlines: ["Guest, 20, Dies After Lake Cabin Party, Friend Charged", "Texts Show Request for 'Half a Blue'"],
        law: "deathByDistribution",
        threshold: 7,
        spec: "Delivered a controlled substance to {V}, whose death was caused by ingesting it, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 19...28,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{V}, 20, was found unresponsive on a couch in a rented lake cabin the morning after a party on {DATE}. The medical examiner found fatal fentanyl. A text from {V} at 10:50 p.m. asked {D} for 'a half of a blue,' and {D} answered 'bringing it.' {V} sent {D} $15 on a payment app labeled 'pizza.' {DL} says {D.he} shared a pill from {D.his} own supply and the $15 was for pizza.",
        state: [E(.digital, 3, "Texts and Payment", "A request for a half pill, a reply, and $15 sent at 11:10 p.m."), E(.forensic, 3, "Medical Examiner", "Fatal fentanyl and a counterfeit pill fragment in {V}'s stomach."), E(.statement, 2, "Party Guest", "A guest saw {D} hand {V} a pill.")],
        defense: [E(.document, 2, "Pizza Receipt", "A delivery receipt for $62 earlier that night, split among guests."), E(.forensic, 1, "Defendant's Blood", "{DL} also tested positive that night.")],
        role: "Sheriff's investigator",
        exam: [.direct("What are your duties as a sheriff's investigator?", "\"I investigate overdose deaths and work with medical examiners. I review messages, payments, and witness statements to find the source of pills.\""), .direct("What happened to {V}?", "\"{V}, who was 20, was found unresponsive on a couch in a rented lake cabin the morning after a party on {DATE}. The medical examiner found fatal fentanyl.\""), .direct("What did {V} text {D}?", "\"At 10:50 p.m., {V} asked for a half of a blue. {D} answered bringing it.\""), .direct("What payment did {V} send?", "\"$15 sent at 11:10 p.m. on a payment app labeled pizza. The app label is not what the payment was for, in my view.\""), .direct("What did a party guest see?", "\"I saw {DL} handing {V} a pill. The guest told me that directly and gave a statement.\""), .direct("What did the medical examiner find in {V}'s stomach?", "\"Fatal fentanyl and a counterfeit pill fragment. The fragment is consistent with a blue pill.\""), .cross("Was there a pizza receipt?", "\"Yes. A delivery receipt for $62 earlier that night, split among guests. That could explain a $15 payment.\""), .cross("Did the defendant also test positive that night?", "\"Yes. {DL} tested positive for fentanyl. {DL} took a pill too, which suggests {DL} did not know.\""), .cross("Where did the defendant get the pills?", "\"From a friend. {D.He} says {D.he} shared a pill from {D.his} own supply and took one that night.\""), .cross("What did the defendant tell another guest?", "\"That {D.he} sold the blues for fifteen each. That is harmful to {D.him}, and I considered it.\""), .cross("Did the defendant try to help {V}?", "\"I understand {DL} was upset the next morning. I cannot say what {DL} did that night.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Cabin guest",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Please tell us about your night at the cabin.", "\"I was a guest at the party. I knew {D} and {V} from school, and we were all having a good time.\""), .direct("What did you see {D} do?", "\"I saw {DF} hand {V} half a pill. It looked like a friendly gesture, and it did not look like a sale.\""), .direct("What did you hear about pizza?", "\"We ordered pizza and split the cost. {V} paid {DF} back for a share, and I saw the delivery.\""), .direct("What was the defendant's condition that night?", "\"{D.He} also took a pill and was sick later. {D.He} was very upset the next day and could not stop crying.\""), .direct("What kind of person is the defendant?", "\"Kind and generous. {DF} shares everything. I never thought of {DF} as a dealer, and I was shocked.\""), .direct("What did you see the next morning?", "\"I saw {V} on the couch and could not wake {V}. I called for help right away.\""), .cross("Did you see the defendant take money for the pill?", "\"No. I did not see a payment. I only know what {D.he} told me about the pizza.\""), .cross("Did the defendant ever say anything about selling pills?", "\"I heard that {D.he} said fifteen each. I did not hear it myself, and I do not know whether it was a joke.\""), .cross("Did you take a pill that night?", "\"No. I did not. I do not take pills, and I stayed away from them.\""), .cross("Did you know the pills were fentanyl?", "\"No. No one at the party did. If we had known, we would not have taken them.\""), .cross("Did {D} bring many pills?", "\"I do not know. I only saw one handed to {V}. I did not look in {DF}'s bag.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} delivered a pill for money and {V} died.", "{D} shared a pill and was paid for pizza."),
        allocution: "\"I did not know what was in it.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} had told another guest {D.he} sold the blues for fifteen each.", "{DL} got the pills from a friend and took one {D.himself} that night."),
        defendant: [.direct("Describe the party at the cabin in your own words.", "\"We were friends gathered at a rented lake cabin. We shared food, music, and some pills. It was meant to be a fun night.\""), .direct("What did you give {V}?", "\"A half pill. {V} asked, and I shared one from my own supply. I thought it was a regular pill.\""), .direct("What was the $15 for?", "\"Pizza. {V} paid me back for a share of the pizza, and the label on the payment says pizza.\""), .direct("Did you sell pills?", "\"I shared them. I told a guest fifteen each, but it was a joke. I did not run a business.\""), .direct("Did you take a pill yourself?", "\"Yes. I took one that night and tested positive. I did not know it held fentanyl, and I could have died too.\""), .direct("How do you feel about what happened?", "\"I would say I feel awful. {V} died, and I gave {V} a pill. I think about it every night, and I wish I could take it back.\""), .cross("You answered bringing it to {V}'s text, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I did. I was bringing a pill. I did not know what was in it.\""), .cross("You told another guest you sold the blues for fifteen each, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I said it as a joke. It was not true, but I realize how that sounds.\""), .cross("$15 is the price you named, isn't it?", "\"It is. But the payment was for pizza. The label says pizza, and so does the receipt.\""), .cross("A guest saw you hand {V} a pill, didn't the guest?", "\"Yes. I handed it over. I am not denying that part.\""), .cross("You got the pills from a friend, didn't you?", "\"Yes. A friend gave them to me. I did not test them, and I know I know I should have.\"")],
        openings: ("{V}, 20, was found unresponsive on a couch in a rented lake cabin the morning after a party on {DATE}. The medical examiner found fatal fentanyl, and a text shows {V} asking {D} for a half of a blue, with $15 sent on a payment app labeled pizza.", "The defense will present a friend who shared a pill from {D}'s own supply, a payment for pizza, and a pill that {D} also took and that made {D} sick. {D} did not know it was fentanyl."),
        closings: ("A request for a half of a blue, a reply of bringing it, $15 at 11:10, a guest who saw the handoff, and fentanyl in {V}'s stomach. {D} said the blues sold for fifteen each.", "A shared pill, a pizza payment, and a friend who took the same pill and got sick. The State has not proved that {D} knew the pill held fentanyl or sold it."),
        timeline: [(0, "7 p.m.: the party begins."), (0, "10:50 p.m.: {V} texts {DL}."), (0, "11:10 p.m.: $15 is sent."), (1, "7 a.m.: {V} is found.")],
        identified: "{V}'s phone and a guest's statement.",
        notDone: ["{DL}'s supplier was never identified."],
        aggravating: ["The offense involved a controlled substance that caused a death"],
        mitigating: ["The defendant was young at the time of the offense", "No prior criminal record"],
        mood: .divided,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof", "lesserIncluded"])

    static let paramedicCashTheftV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.paramedicCashTheft",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Nanny Camera Catches Paramedic Pocketing Bills at Bedside", "Marked Money Found in Locker"],
        law: "felonyLarceny",
        threshold: 7,
        spec: "Took money of {V}, worth over $1,500, while responding to a call as a paramedic, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{V}, an elderly resident, called for help after a fall on {DATE} and left a tin of cash on the nightstand. A nanny camera in the room recorded a paramedic, {D}, taking bills while the other medic was in the hall. Later a marked bill found in {D}'s locker matched {V}'s list. {DL} says another medic or a relative had access to the tin.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Nanny Camera", "A paramedic's hand takes a fold of bills from a tin."), E(.physical, 3, "Marked Bill", "A bill with {V}'s pencil marks found in {DL}'s locker."), E(.document, 1, "Family Report", "The family lists $2,400 missing.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Other Medic", "{DL} says the other medic was also in the room.")],
        role: "Fire department captain",
        exam: [.direct("What does your work as a fire department captain involve?", "\"I lead a team of firefighters and paramedics. I am responsible for our conduct on calls, and I handle complaints when someone says something went wrong.\""), .direct("What happened on {DATE}?", "\"{V}, an elderly resident, called for help after a fall and left a tin of cash on the nightstand. Two medics responded.\""), .direct("What did the nanny camera show?", "\"A paramedic's hand taking a fold of bills from the tin while the other medic was in the hall. The camera was in the room.\""), .direct("How was {D} identified?", "\"The camera shows {D}'s uniform and {D.his} hand. A marked bill with {V}'s pencil marks was found later in {DL}'s locker.\""), .direct("How much was missing?", "\"The family lists $2,400. {V} had counted and marked the bills, and some marked bills turned up.\""), .direct("What did you learn about the defendant's finances?", "\"{D.He} had bills for a debt and was seen counting cash at the station. I noted that.\""), .cross("Was the other medic in the room?", "\"The other medic was in the hall for part of the call and also in the room at other times.\""), .cross("Who had access to the defendant's locker?", "\"The shift partner had a key and a history of complaints. I cannot say that only {DL} could have placed the bill.\""), .cross("Did a relative have access to the tin?", "\"Possibly. The family visited. I cannot say who else touched the tin before the call.\""), .cross("Did the defendant deny taking the cash?", "\"Yes. {D.He} said another medic or a relative had access. {D.He} did not admit it.\""), .cross("Can you see the defendant's face on the video?", "\"I see a uniform and a hand. The camera angle does not show the face clearly.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} took cash from a hurt patient's home.", "The video is unclear and the locker is shared."),
        allocution: "\"I made a terrible choice.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} had bills for a debt and was seen counting cash at the station.", "The shift partner had a key to the locker and a history of complaints."),
        defendant: [.direct("Tell us about your work as a paramedic.", "\"I respond to medical emergencies, many involving the elderly. I take pride in treating patients with respect, and I never took anything before.\""), .direct("What happened at {V}'s home?", "\"We responded to a fall. I treated {V} and helped load {V} into the ambulance. I did not take anything from the tin.\""), .direct("What does the camera show?", "\"A hand taking bills. It is a paramedic's hand, but it was not mine. My partner was also in the room.\""), .direct("Why was a marked bill in your locker?", "\"I cannot say. My partner has a key to the locker and a history of complaints, and I certainly never placed it there.\""), .direct("Why were you counting cash at the station?", "\"I had a debt to pay and was counting my pay. It never crossed my mind that it could look suspicious.\""), .direct("How has this affected you?", "\"I would say I feel hurt and angry. I would never steal from a patient, and I am afraid of losing my career.\""), .cross("You had a debt, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I had bills due. I was struggling, but I did not take {V}'s money.\""), .cross("You were seen counting cash at the station, weren't you?", "\"Yes. It was my own pay. I counted it in front of others, and I did not hide it.\""), .cross("The marked bill was in your locker, wasn't it?", "\"Yes. But my partner had a key, and I cannot explain how the bill got in there.\""), .cross("The camera shows a paramedic's hand taking bills, doesn't it?", "\"Yes. But the hand could be my partner's. We wear the same uniform.\""), .cross("You were in the room while the other medic was in the hall, weren't you?", "\"Yes. For part of the time. I did not take anything, and I did not see anyone else do it.\"")],
        openings: ("{V}, an elderly resident, called for help after a fall on {DATE} and left a tin of cash on the nightstand. A nanny camera recorded a paramedic, {D}, taking bills while the other medic was in the hall, and a marked bill from {V}'s list was found in {D}'s locker.", "The defense will present a second medic who was also in the room, a locker that the shift partner could open, and a hand on camera that could be anyone's in uniform. {D} did not take the money."),
        closings: ("A hand on camera taking a fold of bills, a marked bill with {V}'s pencil marks in {D}'s locker, $2,400 missing, and a debt that {D} was seen counting cash for. The evidence points to {D}.", "A second medic with a key to the locker and a history of complaints, and a camera that shows a hand and not a face. The State has not proved that {D} took the cash."),
