        theory: ("{D} drove drunk on a revoked license.", "A ride fell through and {D} drove only a short way."),
        allocution: "\"I knew better.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} drove to the party in the first place and planned to drive home.", "{DL}'s ride really did cancel by text minutes before."),
        defendant: [.direct("Tell the jury about your evening.", "\"I went to a retirement party. I had a few drinks, and I planned to get a ride home with a friend.\""), .direct("Why did you drive to the store?", "\"My ride cancelled by text minutes before. I needed ice and I thought a short drive would be fine.\""), .direct("Why did you stumble at the register?", "\"I was tired and unsteady. I know I smelled of alcohol. I was ashamed and I should not have driven.\""), .direct("Did you know your license was revoked?", "\"Yes. I knew. I was careless, and I knew I should not drive, even a short way.\""), .direct("What did you say to the deputy?", "\"I told the deputy my ride had fallen through and that I only drove a short way. I was honest.\""), .direct("How are you coping with what happened?", "\"Honestly, I feel stupid. I made a bad choice, and I have a record. I should have called someone else.\""), .cross("You drove to the party in the first place, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I did. I planned to drive home, and I know that was a bad plan.\""), .cross("Your license was revoked for a prior DWI, wasn't it?", "\"Yes. I know. I am not proud of it.\""), .cross("You blew 0.10, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I did. It is over the limit, and I do not dispute it.\""), .cross("You could have called another ride, couldn't you?", "\"Yes. I did not. I thought a short drive would be safe, and I was wrong.\""), .cross("You smelled of alcohol at the store, didn't you?", "\"Yes. The clerk says so. I had been drinking at the party.\"")],
        openings: ("After a retirement party, a store clerk saw {D} stumble at the register at 9:50 p.m. on {DATE} while buying ice and drive away. A deputy stopped {D} at a light, a breath test read 0.10, and {D}'s license was revoked for a prior DWI.", "The defense will present a ride that cancelled by text minutes before, and a short drive to buy ice. {D} accepts what happened and asks the jury to look at the whole evening."),
        closings: ("A clerk who saw {D} stumble and drive away, a breath test of 0.10, and a license revoked for a prior DWI. {D} drove to the party planning to drive home.", "A ride that really did cancel minutes before, and a short drive to a store. The State must prove every element, and the ride shows it was not a plan to drive far."),
