        mood: .indifferent)

    static let eyeDropPoisoningV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.eyeDropPoisoning",
        category: .violent,
        headlines: ["Husband's Kidney Failure Traced to Antifreeze in Sports Drinks", "Wife Charged After Autopsy Finds Crystals"],
        law: "murder1",
        threshold: 11,
        spec: "With premeditation and deliberation, killed {V} by poisoning {V.him} with ethylene glycol.",
        ages: 34...40,
        victim: true,
        summary: "On {DATE}, {V} was taken from the home to an emergency room with kidney failure after days of nausea and confusion, and died two days later. The medical examiner found calcium oxalate crystals in {V}'s kidneys and ethylene glycol, the main part of antifreeze, in {V}'s blood. Store video showed {D}, {V.his} spouse, buying a jug of antifreeze a month earlier. {DL} had also searched for how much it takes to kill an adult and filed for a life insurance payout. {DL} says {V} drank heavily and may have gotten into a garage jug by mistake.",
        state: [E(.forensic, 3, "Autopsy", "Crystals in the kidneys and ethylene glycol in the blood."), E(.digital, 3, "Search History", "{DL}'s searches: 'how much antifreeze kills an adult' and 'does it taste sweet.'"), E(.video, 2, "Store Video", "{DL} buys a gallon of antifreeze and pays cash."), E(.document, 2, "Insurance Claim", "A $500,000 policy claimed within two weeks."), E(.statement, 2, "Recorded Interview", "{DL} says {V} had been 'asking for it.'")],
        defense: [E(.document, 2, "Drinking History", "Medical notes describing {V}'s heavy drinking."), E(.document, 2, "Garage Jug", "A jug of mislabeled antifreeze in the garage that had been used for the car."), E(.statement, 1, "Interview Context", "{DL} was exhausted and grieving during the interview.")],
        role: "Medical examiner",
        exam: [.direct("Tell us about your work as a medical examiner.", "\"I determine causes of death. I perform autopsies, review toxicology, and testify about what the medical evidence shows.\""), .direct("What happened to {V}?", "\"On {DATE}, {V} was taken from the home to an emergency room with kidney failure after days of nausea and confusion. {V} died two days later.\""), .direct("What did the autopsy show?", "\"Calcium oxalate crystals in the kidneys and ethylene glycol in the blood. Ethylene glycol is the main part of antifreeze.\""), .direct("What did the toxicology mean?", "\"The poison caused the kidney failure. It is a recognized pattern, and it matches the days of nausea and confusion.\""), .direct("What did {D}'s search history show?", "\"Searches for how much antifreeze kills an adult and whether it tastes sweet. They were made before {V}'s illness.\""), .direct("What did store video show?", "\"It shows {D} buying a gallon of antifreeze and paying cash about a month earlier.\""), .cross("Could {V} have gotten into a garage jug by mistake?", "\"It is possible. A jug of mislabeled antifreeze was in the garage, and {V} drank heavily. I cannot rule it out.\""), .cross("Did {V} have a drinking history?", "\"Yes. Medical notes describe heavy drinking. A person who drinks heavily may mistake a container.\""), .cross("Did the garage jug carry a label?", "\"A cut-open label showed {V} had been mixing it into radiator water. That suggests {V} handled it.\""), .cross("Was the defendant's statement given while grieving?", "\"Yes. {D.He} was exhausted and grieving during the interview. {D.He} said {V} had been asking for it.\""), .cross("Did you find the defendant giving anything to {V}?", "\"I have no direct evidence. I only know what the tests show, not how the poison got in.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Family doctor",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Tell us about your work as a family doctor.", "\"I treated {V} for years. I know {V}'s history, including heavy drinking and repeated health problems.\""), .direct("What did you note about {V}'s drinking?", "\"Heavy drinking. I counseled {V} several times, and {V} was often confused, even before this illness.\""), .direct("Could a person with that history mistake a container?", "\"Yes. Confusion and drinking can lead to mistakes. I have seen patients drink things by accident.\""), .direct("What did you see of {D}'s care for {V}?", "\"{D} brought {V} to appointments and managed medications. {DF} seemed devoted to {V}.\""), .direct("What did you think when you learned of the poison?", "\"I was shocked. I could not say how it got in. I told investigators about {V}'s history.\""), .direct("What would you tell the jury about the defendant?", "\"{DF} was loving and patient with a hard patient. I never saw anything that made me doubt {DF}.\""), .cross("Did you ever see {V} drink antifreeze?", "\"No. I did not. I only know about {V}'s drinking, not about any antifreeze.\""), .cross("Could {V}'s symptoms have another cause?", "\"Not the crystals and the ethylene glycol. Those point to poison. I cannot say how it got in.\""), .cross("Did the defendant say anything about antifreeze?", "\"No. {D.He} did not mention it to me. I only know what the case says.\""), .cross("Did {V} have a history of mistakes with containers?", "\"Not that I know of. I only know the confusion and the drinking.\""), .cross("Were there days of symptoms before admission?", "\"Yes. Days of nausea and confusion. A person with a poisoning would likely have suffered those days.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} slowly poisoned {D.his} spouse with antifreeze and claimed the insurance.", "A tragic accident by a drinker who found a jug."),
        allocution: "\"I do not know what to say.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} was taking sweetened drinks to {V} each night and keeping the antifreeze receipt.", "The garage jug had a cut-open label that showed {V} had been mixing it into radiator water."),
        defendant: [.direct("Tell us about your marriage.", "\"We were married for years. {V} drank heavily, and it was hard. I cared for {V}, and I tried to help.\""), .direct("Why did you buy antifreeze?", "\"For the car. I paid cash because I often do. It was an ordinary purchase, and a gallon is not unusual.\""), .direct("Why did you search about antifreeze and sweetness?", "\"I read about pet poisoning in the news and wondered. I did not mean anything by it, and I know how it looks.\""), .direct("Did you poison {V}?", "\"No. I did not. I loved {V}, and I would never have done that. I was heartbroken when {V} died.\""), .direct("What did you mean by asking for it?", "\"I was exhausted and grieving. I said something I did not mean in the interview. I did not mean {V} deserved to die.\""), .direct("Why did you file the insurance claim?", "\"The policy was there, and I needed money for the funeral and bills. I did not plan it.\""), .cross("You searched how much antifreeze kills an adult, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I did. It was a poor curiosity, and I know the timing looks bad.\""), .cross("You filed for $500,000 within two weeks, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I did. I was told to file quickly. I know how fast it looks.\""), .cross("You took sweetened drinks to {V} each night, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I did. {V} liked them. I kept the antifreeze receipt because I keep all my receipts.\""), .cross("You said {V} had been asking for it, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I said it. I was exhausted and grieving, and I regret it.\""), .cross("You paid cash for the antifreeze, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I usually pay cash. It was not meant to hide anything.\"")],
        openings: ("On {DATE}, {V} was taken to an emergency room with kidney failure after days of nausea and confusion, and died two days later. The medical examiner found ethylene glycol in {V}'s blood, and store video showed {D}, {V}'s spouse, buying antifreeze a month earlier.", "The defense will present a person who drank heavily, a mislabeled antifreeze jug in the garage, and a spouse who was grieving during an interview. A death with an innocent explanation is not a murder."),
        closings: ("Crystals in the kidneys, ethylene glycol in the blood, searches for how much antifreeze kills an adult, a gallon bought for cash, and a $500,000 claim within two weeks. The evidence fits together.", "A heavy drinker, a mislabeled jug in the garage, and a grieving spouse. The State has not proved that {D} poisoned {V}, and an accident remains possible."),
        timeline: [(-30, "The antifreeze purchase."), (-20, "The searches."), (-4, "{V} grows ill."), (0, "{V} is taken to the emergency room.")],
